# Remove once Spring Boot's BOM reaches tomcat 11.0.25 or later. All three
# entries are the same 11.0.24 -> 11.0.25 bump, and all three are bugs in
# Tomcat's container-managed security: <security-constraint> path matching and
# the DIGEST and FORM authenticator valves. Not exploitable: we ship no
# web.xml and declare no security constraints or Tomcat realm, so those
# authenticators never run. Authentication is Spring Security filter chains
# (API-KEY and Bearer, both stateless), and authorization is enforced in the
# controllers.
CVE-2026-65182
CVE-2026-65905
CVE-2026-68525

# Remove once Spring Boot's BOM reaches jackson 2.21.7 / 3.1.7 or later. All
# five entries hit both 2.21.5 and 3.1.5 and are fixed by that one bump. Each
# needs a databind feature we don't use for untrusted input: String-to-number
# coercion into BigDecimal/BigInteger/Double/Float (no such DTO fields),
# createParser(DataInput) (we never parse from DataInput), XML Duration /
# XMLGregorianCalendar targets (none), @JsonTypeInfo NAME with a defaultImpl
# fallback (LegacyQuery.QueryFilter has none, and FAIL_ON_INVALID_SUBTYPE stays
# on), and @JsonIdentityInfo collections (none).
CVE-2026-89407
CVE-2026-89425
CVE-2026-68497
CVE-2026-91776
CVE-2026-91777
